Description: Include opensslv.h before testing OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER
 Pkcs11Provider.hpp and FileProvider.hpp choose their OpenSSL includes with
 "#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x30000000L" before any OpenSSL header has been
 included, so the macro is undefined, evaluates to 0, and the pre-3.0 branch is
 always taken. That branch includes openssl/engine.h, which Fedora 44's
 OpenSSL 3.5 (configured with no-engine) does not ship, so every translation
 unit that reaches these headers (PKIDH.h, SecurityPluginFactory.cpp) fails
 with "openssl/engine.h: No such file or directory" when Fast DDS is built with
 -DSECURITY=ON. Including openssl/opensslv.h first makes the version test
 meaningful: OpenSSL 3.x and 4.x then take the openssl/types.h branch.
Origin: vendor-specific
Forwarded: no, upstream issue to be filed; the include-order bug is present on upstream master as of 2026-10-26
Last-Update: 2026-10-26
---
--- a/src/cpp/security/artifact_providers/Pkcs11Provider.hpp	2026-10-26 09:00:35.825697330 -0500
+++ b/src/cpp/security/artifact_providers/Pkcs11Provider.hpp	2026-10-26 09:00:35.857761746 -0500
@@ -21,6 +21,11 @@
 
 #include <string>
 
+// opensslv.h defines OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER; without it the test below sees 0
+// and the pre-3.0 branch (openssl/engine.h, absent from OpenSSL builds
+// configured with no-engine) is always taken.
+#include <openssl/opensslv.h>
+
 #if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x30000000L
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
--- a/src/cpp/security/artifact_providers/FileProvider.hpp	2026-10-26 09:00:35.824079980 -0500
+++ b/src/cpp/security/artifact_providers/FileProvider.hpp	2026-10-26 09:00:35.857806336 -0500
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 #include <functional>
 #include <string>
 
+// opensslv.h defines OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER; without it the test below sees 0
+// and the pre-3.0 branch (openssl/engine.h, absent from OpenSSL builds
+// configured with no-engine) is always taken.
+#include <openssl/opensslv.h>
+
 #if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x30000000L
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
